# Mad Cool announces name change and huge site enhancements for 2027

> 🎵 *Curated Music Story from NME Music Official Publications*

### 📖 The Full Story

Mad Cool festival has announced a change to its name, as well as some huge site enhancements in place for 2027.

The Spanish festival is set to return for its 11th edition next summer, following a stacked 2026 line-up that included sets from Pulp , Foo Fighters , Florence & The Machine , and Nick Cave & The Bad Seeds .

Now, organisers have announced that they have made Zurich the first title sponsor in the festival’s history, and have renamed the festival Mad Cool Zurich.

### 🎤 Key Highlights & Community Reactions

The new partnership is described by organisers as a new era, and sees the two brands come together to continue to champion live music and create opportunities to connect with audiences through new experiences and initiatives.

As well as the new name, there are also changes to the festival site, including the introduction of grandstands at its Main Stage. Set to offer new ways to experience the festival, the grandstands let crowds have the opportunity to watch the live performances from a seated position, at no additional cost.

The design also creates a new meeting point within the festival, makes panoramic views of the stage, and includes new areas for relaxation, leisure and food.

Other new features include enhanced audiovisual production, an increase in the number of stages, more shaded areas, additional greenery, new spaces for relaxation.

As seen in previous years, the festival will bring back a layout featuring two parallel Main Stages, alongside four additional stages – maintaining a total of six stages. Larger screens are also being introduced, and there is a new, more ambitious approach to green spaces than in the past.

